      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Presenting the logic behind traditionalist views will actually strengthen your lesson considerably by promoting nuance. Instead of just labeling them \"wrong,\" explore the *values* they were defending, such as stability, order, or community tradition. This approach teaches students to analyze the *underlying reasoning* of a viewpoint, which is a vital historical skill. By doing so, you teach them that even deeply held beliefs come from a specific worldview, making the ultimate judgment more complex and thoughtful.",
      "source": "target",
